{
  "_comment": "Golden prompts for scripts/eval.py --agent vessels: Act 3's one open question (redesign-open-question.md section 3.10). expected_tools is a SUBSEQUENCE of the streamed tool calls; forbidden_text must not appear anywhere in the stream (the agent's words and its tool inputs); forbidden_prose is checked on the words only, since the coverage files a display carries are named unproven_<pass>. expected_inputs, forbidden_inputs, expected_before and expected_after check the calls' inputs ({pass_id} filled from the call they pair with); required_text_by_ending holds the words for a draft and for decide(stop). setup_prompt runs first in the same session and is not checked; every setup is the question, so a follow-up runs after a question closed (review M1). Every pass is on file (scripts/build_vessel_cache.py); nothing here reads radar or AIS live. Gate A runs every case plus --only open-question --repeat 3. The four-turn cases (unseen-in-the-reserve, where-next, draft-tasking) stay on develop and in the act3-four-turn-fallback tag.",
